 \\\\\n3x &= (50 - x) - 6 \\\\\n3x &= 44 - x \\\\\n4x &= 44 \\\\\nx &= 11\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $x=11$ back into the equation $y=50 - x$ to solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= 50 - x \\\\\n&= 50 - 11 \\\\\n&= 39\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to the system is $x=11$ and $y=39$. Therefore, the two numbers are $11$ and $39$." 13194139536831 17592186045436 true] [17592186087446 1074 "Let $x$ be the smaller number and $y$ the larger.\n\n- The sum of the two numbers is $50$, so $x+y=50$.\n- Three times the smaller number is $6$ less than the larger, so $3x=y-6$.\n\nPutting these equations together, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{x + y = 50; 3x = y - 6\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. We solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx + y &= 50 \\\\\ny &= 50 - x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $y=50-x$ into the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x &= y - 6 \\\\\n3x &= (50 - x) - 6 \\\\\n3x &= 44 - x \\\\\n4x &= 44 \\\\\nx &= 11\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $x=11$ back into the equation $y=50 - x$ to solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= 50 - x \\\\\n&= 50 - 11 \\\\\n&= 39\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to the system is $x=11$ and $y=39$. Therefore, the two numbers are $11$ and $39$." 13194139536831 17592186045436 false] [17592186087447 1074 "Let $x$ be the number of marbles that Xander has, and let $y$ be the number of marbles that Yohan has.\n\n- Together, Xander and Yohan have $60$ marbles, so $x+y=60$.\n- Twice the number of marbles that Xander has is $12$ more than the number of marbles that Yohan has, so $2x=y+12$.\n\nPutting these equations together, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}x + y = 60 \\\\ 2 x = y + 12\\end{array} \\right. }\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. We solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx + 