ations together, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{4x = 5y + 26; x + y = 164\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. We solve for $x$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x &= 5y + 26 \\\\\n\\frac{1}{4} \\cdot 4x &= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot (5y + 26) \\\\\nx &= \\frac{5y + 26}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{5y+26}{4}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx + y &= 164 \\\\\n\\frac{5y + 26}{4} + y &= 164 \\\\\n\\frac{5y + 26}{4} + \\frac{4y}{4} &= 164 \\\\\n\\frac{5y + 26 + 4y}{4} &= 164 \\\\\n\\frac{9y + 26}{4} &= 164 \\\\\n9y + 26 &= 656 \\\\\n9y &= 630 \\\\\ny &= 70\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the shorter piece is $70\\,\\textrm{cm}$." 13194139536831 17592186045436 false] [17592186087448 1074 "Let $x$ be the length of the longer piece and let $y$ be the length of the shorter piece.\n\n- Four times the longer is $26\\,\\textrm{cm}$ more than five times the shorter gives $4x=5y+26$.\n- The total length is $164\\,\\textrm{cm}$, so $x+y=164$.\n\nPutting these equations together, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}4 x = 5 y + 26 \\\\ x + y = 164\\end{array} \\right. }\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. We solve for $x$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x &= 5y + 26 \\\\\n\\frac{1}{4} \\cdot 4x &= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot (5y + 26) \\\\\nx &= \\frac{5y + 26}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{5y+26}{4}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx + y &= 164 \\\\\n\\frac{5y + 26}{4} + y &= 164 \\\\\n\\frac{5y + 26}{4} + \\frac{4y}{4} &= 164 \\\\\n\\frac{5y + 26 + 4y}{4} &= 164 \\\\\n\\frac{9y + 26}{4} &= 164 \\\\\n9y + 26 &= 656 \\\\\n9y &= 630 \\\\\ny &= 70\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the shorter piece is $70\\,\\textrm{cm}$." 13194139536831 17592186045436 true] [17592186087449 1074