12375 1080 "0.09 \\mathrm{\\% }" 13194139536831 17592186045436 true] [17592186212375 1080 "0.09%" 13194139536831 17592186045436 false] [17592186212376 1080 "0.12 \\mathrm{\\% }" 13194139536831 17592186045436 true] [17592186212376 1080 "0.12%" 13194139536831 17592186045436 false] [17592186212757 1074 "We're asked to factor the expression\n$(2y - 5)(y - 4) - (2y - 5)(3y + 2)$.\n\nNotice that both terms in this expression contain a common factor of $(2y - 5)$. So, we can factor the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(2y - 5)\\left[(y - 4) - (3y + 2)\\right]\n$$\n\nNow, we simplify the expression inside the square brackets. This gives\n\n$$\n=(2y - 5)(y - 4 - 3y - 2); = (2y - 5)(-2y - 6)\n$$" 13194139536831 17592186045436 false] [17592186212757 1074 "We're asked to factor the expression\n$(2y - 5)(y - 4) - (2y - 5)(3y + 2)$.\n\nNotice that both terms in this expression contain a common factor of $(2y - 5)$. So, we can factor the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(2y - 5)\\left[(y - 4) - (3y + 2)\\right]\n$$\n\nNow, we simplify the expression inside the square brackets. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{array}{rl}\\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  \\phantom{=} ( 2 y - 5 ) ( y - 4 - 3 y - 2 ) \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = ( 2 y - 5 ) ( - 2 y - 6 ) .\\end{array}}\n$$" 13194139536831 17592186045436 true] [17592186212758 1074 "We're asked to factor the expression\n$(2y - 1)(y + 4) + 3(2y - 1)^2$.\n\nNotice that both terms in this expression contain a common factor of $(2y - 1)$. So, we can factor the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(2y - 1)\\left[(y + 4) + 3(2y - 1)\\right]\n$$\n\nNow, we simplify the expression inside the square brackets. This gives\n\n$$\n=(2y - 1)(y + 4 + 6y - 3); = (2y - 1)(7y + 1)\n$$" 13194139536831 17592186045436 false] [17592186212758 1074 "We're asked to factor the expression\n$(2y - 1)(y + 4) + 3(2y - 1)^2$.\n\nNotice that both terms in this expression contain a common factor of $(2y - 1)$. So, we can factor the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(2y - 1)\\left[(y + 4) + 3(2y - 1)\\right]\n$$\n\nNow, we simplify the expression inside the square brackets. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{array}{rl}\\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  \\phantom{=} ( 2 y - 1 ) ( y + 4 + 6 y - 3 ) \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = ( 2 y - 1 ) ( 7 y + 1 ) .\\end{array}}\n$$" 13194139536831 17592186045436 true] [17592186212760 1074 "We're asked to factor the expression\n$(y - 1)^3(y + 2) + (y + 4)(y - 1)^2$.\n\nNotice that both terms in this expression contain a common factor of $(y - 1)^2$. So, we can factor the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(y - 1)^2\\left[(y - 1)(y + 2) + (y + 4)\\right]\n$$\n\nNow, we simplify the expression inside the square brackets. This gives\n\n$$\n=(y - 1)^{2}[(y - 1)(y + 2) + (y + 4)]; = (y - 1)^{2}[y^{2} + y - 2 + y + 4]; = (y - 1)^{2} \\cdot (y^{2} + 2y + 2)_(⏟)_(g(y))\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\ng(y) = y^2 + 2y + 2\n$$" 13194139536831 17592186045436 false] [17592186212760 1074 "We're asked to factor the expression\n$(y - 1)^3(y + 2) + (y + 4)(y - 1)^2$.\n\nNotice that both terms in this expression contain a common factor of $(y - 1)^2$. So, we can factor the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(y - 1)^2\\left[(y - 1)(y + 2) + (y + 4)\\right]\n$$\n\nNow, we simplify the expression inside the square brackets. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{array}{rl}\\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  \\phantom{=} ( y - 1 {)}^{2} [ ( y - 1 ) ( y + 2 ) + ( y + 4 ) ] \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = ( y - 1 {)}^{2} [ {y}^{2} + y - 2 + y + 4 ] \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = ( y - 1 {)}^{2} \\cdot  \\underset{g ( y )}{\\underbrace{( {y}^{2} + 2 y + 2 )}} .\\end{array}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\ng(y) = y^2 + 2y + 2\n$$" 13194139536831 17592186045436 true] [17592186212761 1074 "First, we write the fraction using division:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{64}{x + 3}\\right)}{\\left(\\dfrac{80}{x - 10}\\right)} = \\dfrac{64}{x + 3} \\div \\dfrac{80}{x - 10}\n$$\n\nNext, recall that division is equivalent to multiplication by th